# Game-wide design consistency

Follow `docs/design-contract.md` for every player-facing change.
Before implementing, name the concrete existing reference in the active spec,
state what must remain consistent, and define a comparison in the actual game.
Reuse canonical art, animation and components before inventing replacements.
Joss/Lucas's existing sprites define character design and walking; the rejected
simplified V2 parts are not a new baseline. Jacobo Risa and Spec 019 define the
current environment language. Customization must match in preview and gameplay.
Public login must lead into the authored world, without a technical test room
or the rejected permanent upper character/logout bar.
Compare motion, scale, palette, UI and interactions, not just functional output.
Record real visual evidence and remaining limitations. Technical tests and Web
export never imply visual acceptance or permission to ship a rejected candidate.
Resolve conflicts with current developer direction before changing the affected
contract. Keep routine conforming fixes autonomous; do not repeatedly ask for
permission to follow already established design.
